# 超纲词 2023红宝书考研英语超纲词
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-超纲词
# 描述: 历年考研英语真题中超纲词汇汇总

{{abnormal}}{/æbˈnɔːrml/}}{adj. 异常的；不正常的}}{{The test results showed abnormal levels of cholesterol in his blood.}}

{{abolish}}{/əˈbɒlɪʃ/}}{v. 废除；取消}}{{The government abolished the outdated law in 2020.}}

{{abrupt}}{/əˈbrʌpt/}}{adj. 突然的；唐突的}}{{The abrupt change in weather caught everyone off guard.}}

{{accessory}}{/əkˈsesəri/}}{n. 附件；配件；adj. 辅助的}}{{The store sells手机 accessories such as cases and chargers.}}

{{acclaim}}{/əˈkleɪm/}}{v. 称赞；n. 赞誉}}{{The film was critically acclaimed upon its release.}}

{{afflict}}{/əˈflɪkt/}}{v. 折磨；使苦恼}}{{The region has been afflicted by drought for several years.}}

{{aggregate}}{/ˈæɡrɪɡeɪt/}}{v. 聚合；n. 总数}}{{The aggregate score of the two games determined the winner.}}

{{allegiance}}{/əˈliːdʒəns/}}{n. 忠诚；忠贞}}{{Soldiers swore allegiance to the nation.}}

{{anecdote}}{/ˈænɪkdəʊt/}}{n. 轶事；趣闻}}{{The speaker shared an amusing anecdote from his childhood.}}

{{anomaly}}{/əˈnɒməli/}}{n. 异常；不规则}}{{The scientist studied the anomaly in the data carefully.}}

{{apprehend}}{/ˌæprɪˈhend/}}{v. 逮捕；理解}}{{Police apprehended the suspect after a brief chase.}}

{{apt}}{/æpt/}}{adj. 恰当的；有...倾向的}}{{He is apt to forget important dates.}}

{{ardent}}{/ˈɑːrdnt/}}{adj. 热情的；热烈的}}{{She is an ardent supporter of environmental protection.}}

{{aristocracy}}{/ˌærɪˈstɒkrəsi/}}{n. 贵族；上层社会}}{{The aristocracy controlled most of the land in medieval Europe.}}

{{ascertain}}{/ˌæsərˈteɪn/}}{v. 查明；确定}}{{The police are trying to ascertain the cause of the accident.}}

{{aspiration}}{/ˌæspəˈreɪʃn/}}{n. 抱负；渴望}}{{Her aspiration to become a doctor motivated her to study hard.}}

{{atrocity}}{/əˈtrɒsəti/}}{n. 暴行；残忍}}{{The atrocities committed during the war shocked the world.}}

{{augment}}{/ɔːɡˈment/}}{v. 增加；扩大}}{{The company augmented its workforce to meet the growing demand.}}

{{austere}}{/ɒˈstɪər/}}{adj. 朴素的；严厉的}}{{The monks lived an austere life in the monastery.}}

{{benevolent}}{/bəˈnevələnt/}}{adj. 仁慈的；慈善的}}{{The benevolent donor funded the construction of a new school.}}

{{bibliography}}{/ˌbɪbliˈɒɡrəfi/}}{n. 参考书目；文献目录}}{{The research paper includes an extensive bibliography.}}

{{bureaucratic}}{/ˌbjʊərəˈkrætɪk/}}{adj. 官僚的；官僚主义的}}{{The bureaucratic process delayed the approval of the project.}}

{{calamity}}{/kəˈlæməti/}}{n. 灾难；不幸事件}}{{The earthquake was a calamity that devastated the entire region.}}

{{catalyst}}{/ˈkætəlɪst/}}{n. 催化剂；促进因素}}{{The protest served as a catalyst for political change.}}

{{chronic}}{/ˈkrɒnɪk/}}{adj. 慢性的；长期的}}{{Chronic unemployment is a major concern for the government.}}

{{clandestine}}{/klænˈdestɪn/}}{adj. 秘密的；暗中的}}{{The group held clandestine meetings to plan the operation.}}

{{coalition}}{/ˌkəʊəˈlɪʃn/}}{n. 联盟；联合}}{{The political parties formed a coalition government.}}

{{cognitive}}{/ˈkɒɡnətɪv/}}{adj. 认知的；认识的}}{{Cognitive development is crucial in early childhood.}}

{{coherence}}{/kəʊˈhɪərəns/}}{n. 连贯性；一致性}}{{The essay lacks coherence and needs to be revised.}}

{{compelling}}{/kəmˈpelɪŋ/}}{adj. 引人注目的；令人信服的}}{{The documentary presents a compelling argument for reform.}}

{{complacent}}{/kəmˈpleɪsnt/}}{adj. 自满的；得意的}}{{The team became complacent after winning several matches.}}

{{concession}}{/kənˈseʃn/}}{n. 让步；特许权}}{{Both sides made concessions to reach the agreement.}}

{{confiscate}}{/ˈkɒnfɪskeɪt/}}{v. 没收；充公}}{{The customs officer confiscated the prohibited goods.}}

{{congestion}}{/kənˈdʒestʃən/}}{n. 拥挤；堵塞}}{{Traffic congestion is a daily problem in major cities.}}

{{conjecture}}{/kənˈdʒektʃər/}}{n. 推测；猜想}}{{The theory is based on conjecture rather than solid evidence.}}

{{conscientious}}{/ˌkɒnʃiˈenʃəs/}}{adj. 认真的；尽责的}}{{She is a conscientious worker who never cuts corners.}}

{{consecutive}}{/kənˈsekjətɪv/}}{adj. 连续的}}{{The company reported losses for three consecutive quarters.}}

{{conundrum}}{/kəˈnʌndrəm/}}{n. 难题；谜题}}{{The ethical conundrum has no easy answer.}}

{{converge}}{/kənˈvɜːrdʒ/}}{v. 汇聚；趋同}}{{Technology and art are converging in new and exciting ways.}}

{{conviction}}{/kənˈvɪkʃn/}}{n. 定罪；信念}}{{She spoke with conviction about the importance of education.}}

{{corroborate}}{/kəˈrɒbəreɪt/}}{v. 证实；支持}}{{The witness's testimony corroborated the evidence presented.}}

{{counterfeit}}{/ˈkaʊntərfɪt/}}{adj. 伪造的；n. 赝品}}{{The police seized counterfeit currency worth millions.}}

{{covert}}{/ˈkʌvərt/}}{adj. 秘密的；隐蔽的}}{{The government conducted covert operations abroad.}}

{{culminate}}{/ˈkʌlmɪneɪt/}}{v. 达到高潮；告终}}{{Years of hard work culminated in winning the championship.}}

{{cumulative}}{/ˈkjuːmjələtɪv/}}{adj. 累积的；累计的}}{{The cumulative effect of pollution is devastating to the environment.}}

{{curtail}}{/kɜːrˈteɪl/}}{v. 削减；缩减}}{{The company curtailed its spending during the recession.}}

{{daunting}}{/ˈdɔːntɪŋ/}}{adj. 令人畏惧的；令人气馁的}}{{The prospect of starting over was daunting but exciting.}}

{{debacle}}{/deɪˈbɑːkl/}}{n. 惨败；崩溃}}{{The product launch was a complete debacle.}}

{{debris}}{/ˈdebriː/}}{n. 碎片；残骸}}{{The street was covered with debris after the explosion.}}

{{decadence}}{/ˈdekədəns/}}{n. 堕落；颓废}}{{The empire's decline was marked by moral decadence.}}

{{deficit}}{/ˈdefɪsɪt/}}{n. 赤字；不足}}{{The government is working to reduce the budget deficit.}}

{{defy}}{/dɪˈfaɪ/}}{v. 违抗；蔑视}}{{The protesters defied the ban on public gatherings.}}

{{degenerate}}{/dɪˈdʒenəreɪt/}}{v. 退化；堕落}}{{The discussion degenerated into a heated argument.}}

{{detrimental}}{/ˌdetrɪˈmentl/}}{adj. 有害的；不利的}}{{Excessive screen time is detrimental to children's eyesight.}}

{{deviate}}{/ˈdiːvieɪt/}}{v. 偏离；背离}}{{The pilot had to deviate from the planned route due to storms.}}

{{dexterity}}{/dekˈsterəti/}}{n. 灵巧；敏捷}}{{The surgeon's dexterity was crucial during the delicate operation.}}

{{diabolic}}{/ˌdaɪəˈbɒlɪk/}}{adj. 恶魔般的；残忍的}}{{The villain's diabolic plan was foiled by the hero.}}

{{dichotomy}}{/daɪˈkɒtəmi/}}{n. 二分法；对立}}{{There is a dichotomy between theory and practice in education.}}

{{diligent}}{/ˈdɪlɪdʒənt/}}{adj. 勤奋的；勤勉的}}{{The diligent student earned top marks in every subject.}}

{{dismantle}}{/dɪsˈmæntl/}}{v. 拆除；解散}}{{The old factory was dismantled to make way for a new park.}}

{{disparity}}{/dɪˈspærəti/}}{n. 差异；不平等}}{{There is a significant disparity in income between the rich and poor.}}

{{disposition}}{/ˌdɪspəˈzɪʃn/}}{n. 性情；倾向}}{{She has a cheerful disposition that brightens everyone's day.}}

{{dissipate}}{/ˈdɪsɪpeɪt/}}{v. 消散；浪费}}{{The fog dissipated as the sun rose higher.}}

{{dwindle}}{/ˈdwaɪndl/}}{v. 减少；缩小}}{{The population of the island has dwindled over the past century.}}

{{eccentric}}{/ɪkˈsentrɪk/}}{adj. 古怪的；n. 怪人}}{{The eccentric professor was known for his unusual teaching methods.}}

{{edify}}{/ˈedɪfaɪ/}}{v. 启迪；开导}}{{The documentary was designed to edify and inform the public.}}

{{eloquent}}{/ˈeləkwənt/}}{adj. 雄辩的；有说服力的}}{{She gave an eloquent speech that moved the audience to tears.}}

{{emancipate}}{/ɪˈmænsɪpeɪt/}}{v. 解放；使自由}}{{The movement sought to emancipate women from social restrictions.}}

{{eminent}}{/ˈemɪnənt/}}{adj. 杰出的；著名的}}{{The eminent scientist received the Nobel Prize for his discoveries.}}

{{empirical}}{/ɪmˈpɪrɪkl/}}{adj. 经验的；实证的}}{{The study relies on empirical data rather than theory.}}

{{engender}}{/ɪnˈdʒendər/}}{v. 产生；引起}}{{The policy change engendered widespread public debate.}}

{{enmity}}{/ˈenməti/}}{n. 敌意；仇恨}}{{There was long-standing enmity between the two families.}}

{{ephemeral}}{/ɪˈfemərəl/}}{adj. 短暂的；瞬息的}}{{The beauty of cherry blossoms is ephemeral, lasting only a few days.}}

{{equitable}}{/ˈekwɪtəbl/}}{adj. 公平的；公正的}}{{The goal is to create a more equitable distribution of resources.}}

{{eradicate}}{/ɪˈrædɪkeɪt/}}{v. 根除；消灭}}{{The campaign aims to eradicate poverty in the region.}}

{{erratic}}{/ɪˈrætɪk/}}{adj. 不稳定的；古怪的}}{{His erratic behavior worried his colleagues.}}

{{exacerbate}}{/ɪɡˈzæsərbeɪt/}}{v. 加剧；恶化}}{{The drought exacerbated the food shortage in the region.}}

{{exonerate}}{/ɪɡˈzɒnəreɪt/}}{v. 免罪；开释}}{{New evidence exonerated the wrongly convicted man.}}

{{extravagant}}{/ɪkˈstrævəɡənt/}}{adj. 奢侈的；过分的}}{{The wedding was extravagant, with no expense spared.}}

{{fabrication}}{/ˌfæbrɪˈkeɪʃn/}}{n. 捏造；制造}}{{The story turned out to be a complete fabrication.}}

{{facet}}{/ˈfæsɪt/}}{n. 方面；侧面}}{{The problem has many facets that need to be considered.}}

{{fallacy}}{/ˈfæləsi/}}{n. 谬误；错误观念}}{{The argument is based on a common logical fallacy.}}

{{fervent}}{/ˈfɜːrvənt/}}{adj. 热烈的；热情的}}{{The fans gave the team a fervent welcome upon their return.}}

{{flaw}}{/flɔː/}}{n. 缺陷；瑕疵}}{{The flaw in the design was discovered during testing.}}

{{flourish}}{/ˈflʌrɪʃ/}}{v. 繁荣；茂盛}}{{The small business flourished under new management.}}

{{formidable}}{/ˈfɔːrmɪdəbl/}}{adj. 强大的；令人敬畏的}}{{The company faces formidable competition in the global market.}}

{{frugal}}{/ˈfruːɡl/}}{adj. 节俭的；朴素的}}{{She lives a frugal life, saving most of her income.}}

{{futility}}{/fjuːˈtɪləti/}}{n. 无用；徒劳}}{{He realized the futility of arguing with someone who refused to listen.}}

{{garrison}}{/ˈɡærɪsn/}}{n. 驻军；卫戍部队}}{{The garrison defended the fort against the invaders.}}

{{genocide}}{/ˈdʒenəsaɪd/}}{n. 种族灭绝}}{{The United Nations was formed partly to prevent genocide.}}

{{gratitude}}{/ˈɡrætɪtjuːd/}}{n. 感激；感谢}}{{She showed her gratitude by writing a heartfelt thank-you letter.}}

{{gregarious}}{/ɡrɪˈɡeəriəs/}}{adj. 爱交际的；合群的}}{{He is a gregarious person who enjoys social gatherings.}}

{{hamper}}{/ˈhæmpər/}}{v. 妨碍；阻碍}}{{The investigation was hampered by a lack of evidence.}}

{{herald}}{/ˈherəld/}}{v. 预示；n. 先驱}}{{The invention of the printing press heralded a new era of knowledge.}}

{{heresy}}{/ˈherəsi/}}{n. 异端邪说}}{{His views were considered heresy by the religious establishment.}}

{{hierarchy}}{/ˈhaɪərɑːrki/}}{n. 等级制度；层次结构}}{{The company has a严格的 hierarchy with clear lines of authority.}}

{{hypothesis}}{/haɪˈpɒθəsɪs/}}{n. 假设；假说}}{{The researchers proposed a hypothesis to explain the phenomenon.}}

{{idiosyncrasy}}{/ˌɪdiəˈsɪŋkrəsi/}}{n. 特质；癖好}}{{Everyone has their own idiosyncrasies that make them unique.}}

{{impervious}}{/ɪmˈpɜːrviəs/}}{adj. 不受影响的；不能渗透的}}{{He seemed impervious to criticism from his peers.}}

{{impetus}}{/ˈɪmpɪtəs/}}{n. 动力；推动力}}{{The success of the first project provided impetus for further research.}}

{{impoverish}}{/ɪmˈpɒvərɪʃ/}}{v. 使贫穷；使枯竭}}{{Years of war impoverished the once-thriving nation.}}

{{inadvertent}}{/ˌɪnədˈvɜːrtənt/}}{adj. 无意的；疏忽的}}{{The error was inadvertent and was corrected immediately.}}

{{incite}}{/ɪnˈsaɪt/}}{v. 煽动；激起}}{{The speech incited the crowd to protest against the government.}}

{{incongruous}}{/ɪnˈkɒŋɡruəs/}}{adj. 不协调的；不一致的}}{{The modern building looked incongruous among the ancient temples.}}

{{incumbent}}{/ɪnˈkʌmbənt/}}{adj. 在职的；n. 在职者}}{{The incumbent president won re-election by a narrow margin.}}

{{indictment}}{/ɪnˈdaɪtmənt/}}{n. 起诉书；控告}}{{The grand jury issued an indictment against the accused.}}

{{indigenous}}{/ɪnˈdɪdʒənəs/}}{adj. 本土的；土著的}}{{The indigenous people have lived in the region for thousands of years.}}

{{indignation}}{/ˌɪndɪɡˈneɪʃn/}}{n. 愤慨；义愤}}{{The unfair decision caused widespread indignation among the workers.}}

{{infallible}}{/ɪnˈfæləbl/}}{adj. 绝对可靠的；不会犯错的}}{{No one is infallible; everyone makes mistakes.}}

{{infamous}}{/ˈɪnfəməs/}}{adj. 声名狼藉的；臭名昭著的}}{{The criminal was infamous for his series of robberies.}}

{{ingenious}}{/ɪnˈdʒiːniəs/}}{adj. 巧妙的；有创意的}}{{The engineer came up with an ingenious solution to the problem.}}

{{inquisitive}}{/ɪnˈkwɪzətɪv/}}{adj. 好奇的；好问的}}{{The inquisitive child asked questions about everything.}}

{{insidious}}{/ɪnˈsɪdiəs/}}{adj. 阴险的；暗中为害的}}{{The insidious effects of pollution are often not immediately apparent.}}

{{intact}}{/ɪnˈtækt/}}{adj. 完整的；未受损的}}{{Despite the explosion, the building remained largely intact.}}

{{intermittent}}{/ˌɪntərˈmɪtənt/}}{adj. 间歇的；断断续续的}}{{The region experiences intermittent rainfall throughout the year.}}

{{intrusive}}{/ɪnˈtruːsɪv/}}{adj. 侵入的；打扰的}}{{The new regulations were seen as intrusive by many businesses.}}

{{invoke}}{/ɪnˈvəʊk/}}{v. 援引；唤起}}{{The lawyer invoked the First Amendment in his defense.}}

{{irate}}{/aɪˈreɪt/}}{adj. 愤怒的；暴怒的}}{{The irate customer demanded to speak to the manager.}}

{{itinerant}}{/aɪˈtɪnərənt/}}{adj. 巡回的；流动的}}{{The itinerant musician performed in cities across the country.}}

{{juxtapose}}{/ˌdʒʌkstəˈpəʊz/}}{v. 并列；并置}}{{The artist juxtaposed images of war and peace in the mural.}}

{{lament}}{/ləˈment/}}{v. 哀叹；n. 挽歌}}{{She lamented the loss of traditional crafts in the modern era.}}

{{languish}}{/ˈlæŋɡwɪʃ/}}{v. 衰弱；萎靡}}{{The economy languished for years without any signs of recovery.}}

{{laudable}}{/ˈlɔːdəbl/}}{adj. 值得称赞的；可嘉的}}{{Her efforts to improve literacy rates are laudable.}}

{{lethargy}}{/ˈleθərdʒi/}}{n. 昏睡；无精打采}}{{The hot weather induced a sense of lethargy in everyone.}}

{{leverage}}{/ˈlevərɪdʒ/}}{n. 杠杆作用；v. 利用}}{{The company leveraged its brand to enter new markets.}}

{{litigation}}{/ˌlɪtɪˈɡeɪʃn/}}{n. 诉讼；起诉}}{{The company faced litigation over patent infringement.}}

{{loathsome}}{/ˈləʊðsəm/}}{adj. 令人厌恶的；可憎的}}{{The crime was so loathsome that it shocked the entire community.}}

{{lopsided}}{/ˌlɒpˈsaɪdɪd/}}{adj. 不平衡的；倾向一方的}}{{The election resulted in a lopsided victory for the incumbent.}}

{{lucid}}{/ˈluːsɪd/}}{adj. 清晰的；明了的}}{{Despite her illness, she remained lucid and articulate.}}

{{lucrative}}{/ˈluːkrətɪv/}}{adj. 有利可图的；赚钱的}}{{The tech industry offers lucrative career opportunities.}}

{{malaise}}{/mæˈleɪz/}}{n. 不适；萎靡不振}}{{An economic malaise settled over the region after the factory closures.}}

{{malpractice}}{/ˌmælˈpræktɪs/}}{n. 渎职；不当行为}}{{The doctor was sued for medical malpractice.}}

{{mandate}}{/ˈmændeɪt/}}{n. 授权；命令；v. 强制}}{{The government mandated the use of seat belts in all vehicles.}}

{{manifold}}{/ˈmænɪfəʊld/}}{adj. 多种多样的；n. 歧管}}{{The benefits of exercise are manifold.}}

{{mar}}{/mɑːr/}}{v. 损坏；破坏}}{{The beautiful landscape was marred by the construction site.}}

{{meager}}{/ˈmiːɡər/}}{adj. 贫乏的；不足的}}{{The family survived on a meager income.}}

{{mercurial}}{/mɜːrˈkjʊəriəl/}}{adj. 善变的；反复无常的}}{{Her mercurial temperament made her difficult to work with.}}

{{metamorphosis}}{/ˌmetəˈmɔːrfəsɪs/}}{n. 变态；变形}}{{The caterpillar undergoes a metamorphosis to become a butterfly.}}

{{meticulous}}{/məˈtɪkjələs/}}{adj. 一丝不苟的；细致的}}{{The meticulous researcher left no stone unturned in her investigation.}}

{{mollify}}{/ˈmɒlɪfaɪ/}}{v. 安抚；平息}}{{The company offered a refund to mollify the angry customers.}}

{{morose}}{/məˈrəʊs/}}{adj. 忧郁的；阴沉的}}{{He became morose after losing his job.}}

{{mundane}}{/mʌnˈdeɪn/}}{adj. 平凡的；世俗的}}{{She longed for adventure to escape her mundane routine.}}

{{negligence}}{/ˈneɡlɪdʒəns/}}{n. 疏忽；过失}}{{The accident was caused by the negligence of the driver.}}

{{nominal}}{/ˈnɒmɪnl/}}{adj. 名义上的；微不足道的}}{{The fee is nominal compared to the benefits you receive.}}

{{nurture}}{/ˈnɜːrtʃər/}}{v. 培育；n. 养育}}{{Parents play a crucial role in nurturing their children's talents.}}

{{oblivious}}{/əˈblɪviəs/}}{adj. 不知道的；未察觉的}}{{He was oblivious to the danger that surrounded him.}}

{{obnoxious}}{/əbˈnɒkʃəs/}}{adj. 令人不快的；讨厌的}}{{His obnoxious behavior at the party offended many guests.}}

{{obsolete}}{/ˈɒbsəliːt/}}{adj. 过时的；废弃的}}{{The old technology has become obsolete in the modern era.}}

{{ominous}}{/ˈɒmɪnəs/}}{adj. 不祥的；预兆的}}{{The dark clouds were an ominous sign of the approaching storm.}}

{{opaque}}{/əʊˈpeɪk/}}{adj. 不透明的；难懂的}}{{The company's opaque financial practices raised concerns among investors.}}

{{opulent}}{/ˈɒpjələnt/}}{adj. 豪华的；富裕的}}{{The opulent palace was filled with priceless works of art.}}

{{oscillate}}{/ˈɒsɪleɪt/}}{v. 摆动；犹豫}}{{Public opinion oscillated between support and opposition.}}

{{ostensible}}{/ɒˈstensəbl/}}{adj. 表面上的；假装的}}{{The ostensible reason for the meeting was budget review.}}

{{ostracize}}{/ˈɒstrəsaɪz/}}{v. 排斥；放逐}}{{The community ostracized the whistleblower for speaking out.}}

{{paradigm}}{/ˈpærədaɪm/}}{n. 范式；典范}}{{The discovery represented a paradigm shift in the field of biology.}}

{{paramount}}{/ˈpærəmaʊnt/}}{adj. 至高无上的；最重要的}}{{Safety is paramount in the operation of nuclear power plants.}}

{{partisan}}{/ˌpɑːrtɪˈzæn/}}{adj. 党派的；n. 支持者}}{{The debate became increasingly partisan and unproductive.}}

{{patronize}}{/ˈpætrənaɪz/}}{v. 赞助；以高人一等的态度对待}}{{She patronizes local businesses by shopping there regularly.}}

{{penchant}}{/ˈpentʃənt/}}{n. 嗜好；倾向}}{{He has a penchant for classical music.}}

{{peripheral}}{/pəˈrɪfərəl/}}{adj. 外围的；次要的}}{{The issue is peripheral to the main topic of discussion.}}

{{permeate}}{/ˈpɜːrmieɪt/}}{v. 渗透；弥漫}}{{The smell of coffee permeated the entire办公室.}}

{{perpetuate}}{/pəˈpetʃueɪt/}}{v. 使永久化；使持续}}{{The stereotype is perpetuated by media representations.}}

{{pertinent}}{/ˈpɜːrtɪnənt/}}{adj. 相关的；切题的}}{{Please ask questions pertinent to the topic under discussion.}}

{{philanthropy}}{/fɪˈlænθrəpi/}}{n. 慈善；慈善事业}}{{His philanthropy has funded schools and hospitals in developing countries.}}

{{piety}}{/ˈpaɪəti/}}{n. 虔诚；孝顺}}{{Her piety was evident in her daily prayers and charitable acts.}}

{{plausible}}{/ˈplɔːzəbl/}}{adj. 似乎合理的；貌似可信的}}{{The explanation sounds plausible but needs further verification.}}

{{plethora}}{/ˈpleθərə/}}{n. 过多；过剩}}{{The store offers a plethora of choices for consumers.}}

{{polarize}}{/ˈpəʊləraɪz/}}{v. 使两极化}}{{The issue has polarized public opinion across the country.}}

{{pragmatic}}{/præɡˈmætɪk/}}{adj. 务实的；实际的}}{{She took a pragmatic approach to solving the problem.}}

{{precarious}}{/prɪˈkeəriəs/}}{adj. 不稳定的；危险的}}{{The company is in a precarious financial situation.}}

{{predominant}}{/prɪˈdɒmɪnənt/}}{adj. 主要的；占优势的}}{{English is the predominant language used in international business.}}

{{preposterous}}{/prɪˈpɒstərəs/}}{adj. 荒谬的；可笑的}}{{The idea that the earth is flat is preposterous.}}

{{prevalent}}{/ˈprevələnt/}}{adj. 流行的；普遍的}}{{Obesity is increasingly prevalent in developed countries.}}

{{pristine}}{/ˈprɪstiːn/}}{adj. 原始的；纯净的}}{{The island has pristine beaches untouched by tourism.}}

{{prolific}}{/prəˈlɪfɪk/}}{adj. 多产的；丰富的}}{{The prolific author published over thirty novels in her career.}}

{{propensity}}{/prəˈpensəti/}}{n. 倾向；癖好}}{{He has a propensity to take risks in business ventures.}}

{{proprietary}}{/prəˈpraɪətəri/}}{adj. 专有的；专利的}}{{The company uses proprietary technology in its products.}}

{{prospective}}{/prəˈspektɪv/}}{adj. 预期的；未来的}}{{Prospective students should submit their applications by March.}}

{{provisional}}{/prəˈvɪʒənl/}}{adj. 暂时的；临时的}}{{A provisional government was established after the revolution.}}

{{provocative}}{/prəˈvɒkətɪv/}}{adj. 挑衅的；发人深省的}}{{The artist's provocative work sparked intense debate.}}

{{prudent}}{/ˈpruːdnt/}}{adj. 谨慎的；明智的}}{{It would be prudent to save money for unexpected expenses.}}

{{punitive}}{/ˈpjuːnɪtɪv/}}{adj. 惩罚性的}}{{The court imposed punitive damages on the defendant.}}

{{quandary}}{/ˈkwɒndəri/}}{n. 困惑；进退两难}}{{She was in a quandary about whether to accept the job offer.}}

{{rationale}}{/ˌræʃəˈnɑːl/}}{n. 基本原理；理由}}{{The rationale behind the decision was explained in the report.}}

{{rebuff}}{/rɪˈbʌf/}}{v. 断然拒绝；n. 冷落}}{{The proposal was rebuffed by the committee.}}

{{reconciliation}}{/ˌrekənsɪliˈeɪʃn/}}{n. 和解；调和}}{{The two countries worked toward reconciliation after years of conflict.}}

{{rectify}}{/ˈrektɪfaɪ/}}{v. 纠正；修正}}{{The company took steps to rectify the errors in the report.}}

{{redundant}}{/rɪˈdʌndənt/}}{adj. 多余的；被裁员的}}{{The new system made many manual processes redundant.}}

{{relinquish}}{/rɪˈlɪŋkwɪʃ/}}{v. 放弃；交出}}{{He reluctantly relinquished control of the company.}}

{{reminisce}}{/ˌremɪˈnɪs/}}{v. 回忆；追忆}}{{They reminisced about their college days over dinner.}}

{{repercussion}}{/ˌriːpərˈkʌʃn/}}{n. 后果；影响}}{{The decision had far-reaching repercussions for the entire industry.}}

{{replenish}}{/rɪˈplenɪʃ/}}{v. 补充；重新装满}}{{The body needs to replenish its energy stores after exercise.}}

{{reprisal}}{/rɪˈpraɪzl/}}{n. 报复；报复行动}}{{Workers feared reprisals if they reported safety violations.}}

{{residual}}{/rɪˈzɪdʒuəl/}}{adj. 残余的；剩余的}}{{There were residual effects from the medication weeks later.}}

{{resilient}}{/rɪˈzɪliənt/}}{adj. 有弹性的；恢复力强的}}{{Children are remarkably resilient and can adapt to change quickly.}}

{{resonance}}{/ˈrezənəns/}}{n. 共鸣；回响}}{{The speech had a deep resonance with the audience.}}

{{retaliate}}{/rɪˈtælieɪt/}}{v. 报复；反击}}{{The country threatened to retaliate against trade sanctions.}}

{{retrospect}}{/ˈretrəspekt/}}{n. 回顾；追溯}}{{In retrospect, the decision to invest was the right one.}}

{{rhetoric}}{/ˈretərɪk/}}{n. 修辞；言辞}}{{Political rhetoric often simplifies complex issues.}}

{{rigorous}}{/ˈrɪɡərəs/}}{adj. 严格的；严密的}}{{The experiment was conducted under rigorous conditions.}}

{{robust}}{/rəˈbʌst/}}{adj. 强健的；坚固的}}{{The economy showed robust growth in the last quarter.}}

{{safeguard}}{/ˈseɪfɡɑːrd/}}{v. 保护；n. 保障措施}}{{Laws are designed to safeguard the rights of citizens.}}

{{sanction}}{/ˈsæŋkʃn/}}{n. 制裁；认可；v. 批准}}{{The United Nations imposed sanctions on the country.}}

{{scarcity}}{/ˈskeərsəti/}}{n. 缺乏；稀缺}}{{The scarcity of clean water is a global concern.}}

{{scrutiny}}{/ˈskruːtəni/}}{n. 仔细审查；监视}}{{The government's actions came under intense public scrutiny.}}

{{sedentary}}{/ˈsedntri/}}{adj. 久坐不动的}}{{A sedentary lifestyle increases the risk of heart disease.}}

{{skeptical}}{/ˈskeptɪkl/}}{adj. 怀疑的；多疑的}}{{Many scientists were skeptical of the new theory at first.}}

{{solidarity}}{/ˌsɒlɪˈdærəti/}}{n. 团结；一致}}{{The community showed solidarity in the face of the disaster.}}

{{sophistication}}{/səˌfɪstɪˈkeɪʃn/}}{n. 复杂；老练}}{{The sophistication of the technology impressed the visitors.}}

{{sporadic}}{/spəˈrædɪk/}}{adj. 零星的；不定时的}}{{Sporadic gunfire could be heard in the distance.}}

{{stagnant}}{/ˈstæɡnənt/}}{adj. 停滞的；不流动的}}{{The economy remained stagnant for several years.}}

{{stigma}}{/ˈstɪɡmə/}}{n. 耻辱；污名}}{{There is still a stigma attached to mental illness in some societies.}}

{{strategic}}{/strəˈtiːdʒɪk/}}{adj. 战略的；策略的}}{{The company made a strategic decision to expand into Asia.}}

{{stringent}}{/ˈstrɪndʒənt/}}{adj. 严格的；严厉的}}{{The country has stringent regulations on food safety.}}

{{subsidize}}{/ˈsʌbsɪdaɪz/}}{v. 补贴；资助}}{{The government subsidizes renewable energy projects.}}

{{substantiate}}{/səbˈstænʃieɪt/}}{v. 证实；证明}}{{The claims were not substantiated by any evidence.}}

{{subtle}}{/ˈsʌtl/}}{adj. 微妙的；精巧的}}{{The artist used subtle shades of color in the painting.}}

{{succumb}}{/səˈkʌm/}}{v. 屈服；死亡}}{{Many patients succumbed to the disease before a cure was found.}}

{{superfluous}}{/suːˈpɜːrfluəs/}}{adj. 多余的；过剩的}}{{Please remove any superfluous details from the report.}}

{{suppress}}{/səˈpres/}}{v. 压制；镇压}}{{The government attempted to suppress the dissent.}}

{{susceptible}}{/səˈseptəbl/}}{adj. 易受影响的；易感的}}{{Children are more susceptible to infections than adults.}}

{{tangible}}{/ˈtændʒəbl/}}{adj. 有形的；可触摸的}}{{The project has produced tangible results in a short time.}}

{{tentative}}{/ˈtentətɪv/}}{adj. 暂定的；试探的}}{{The two sides reached a tentative agreement on the contract.}}

{{tenure}}{/ˈtenjər/}}{n. 任期；终身教职}}{{The professor was granted tenure after years of exemplary service.}}

{{terminate}}{/ˈtɜːrmɪneɪt/}}{v. 终止；结束}}{{The contract was terminated due to a breach of terms.}}

{{terrestrial}}{/təˈrestriəl/}}{adj. 陆地的；地球的}}{{Terrestrial ecosystems are affected by climate change.}}

{{therapeutic}}{/ˌθerəˈpjuːtɪk/}}{adj. 治疗的；有疗效的}}{{Music has therapeutic effects on people with anxiety.}}

{{thorough}}{/ˈθʌrə/}}{adj. 彻底的；仔细的}}{{The detective conducted a thorough investigation of the crime scene.}}

{{threshold}}{/ˈθreʃhəʊld/}}{n. 门槛；起点}}{{The temperature exceeded the threshold for safe operation.}}

{{transient}}{/ˈtrænziənt/}}{adj. 短暂的；临时的}}{{The transient nature of fame is well documented.}}

{{transplant}}{/trænsˈplɑːnt/}}{v. 移植；n. 移植物}}{{The surgeon successfully transplanted the kidney into the patient.}}

{{trivial}}{/ˈtrɪviəl/}}{adj. 琐碎的；不重要的}}{{Do not waste time on trivial matters.}}

{{tumultuous}}{/tjuːˈmʌltʃuəs/}}{adj. 动荡的；喧闹的}}{{The country经历了一场 tumultuous period of political change.}}

{{ubiquitous}}{/juːˈbɪkwɪtəs/}}{adj. 无处不在的}}{{Smartphones have become ubiquitous in modern society.}}

{{unprecedented}}{/ʌnˈpresɪdentɪd/}}{adj. 前所未有的；空前的}}{{The pandemic caused unprecedented disruption to the global economy.}}

{{utilitarian}}{/ˌjuːtɪlɪˈteəriən/}}{adj. 功利的；实用的}}{{The design is utilitarian rather than aesthetically pleasing.}}

{{vanguard}}{/ˈvæŋɡɑːrd/}}{n. 先锋；先驱}}{{The company is at the vanguard of technological innovation.}}

{{vehement}}{/ˈviːəmənt/}}{adj. 激烈的；强烈的}}{{She expressed vehement opposition to the proposed changes.}}

{{venerable}}{/ˈvenərəbl/}}{adj. 值得尊敬的；古老的}}{{The venerable institution has been educating students for over 200 years.}}

{{versatile}}{/ˈvɜːrsətaɪl/}}{adj. 多才多艺的；多功能的}}{{She is a versatile actress who can play any role convincingly.}}

{{viable}}{/ˈvaɪəbl/}}{adj. 可行的；能生存的}}{{Solar power is a viable alternative to fossil fuels.}}

{{vigilant}}{/ˈvɪdʒɪlənt/}}{adj. 警觉的；警惕的}}{{The security team remained vigilant throughout the event.}}

{{vilify}}{/ˈvɪlɪfaɪ/}}{v. 诽谤；中伤}}{{The media vilified the politician after the scandal.}}

{{vindicate}}{/ˈvɪndɪkeɪt/}}{v. 证明...正确；为...辩护}}{{The new evidence vindicated the scientist's original theory.}}

{{volatile}}{/ˈvɒlətaɪl/}}{adj. 不稳定的；易变的}}{{The stock market has been volatile in recent weeks.}}

{{warrant}}{/ˈwɒrənt/}}{n. 授权令；v. 保证}}{{The police obtained a warrant to search the premises.}}

{{zealous}}{/ˈzeləs/}}{adj. 热情的；狂热的}}{{The zealous volunteers worked tirelessly to help the community.}}
